WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.740
[Swing jazz music]

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.360
[Niko:] Is it time?

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.360
[Sam:] It's finally time

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.300
[Niko:] Here we go

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.500
[Sam:] Today's a big day

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.020
because in February of 2011 we started this little channel called

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.140
"Sam and Niko"

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.020
Featuring yours truly and his truly

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:20.280
but you know what, it's been a few years and since then

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:21.700
The team has grown

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.520
It's not really about us anymore. It's about everyone here. It's about the whole crew.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.340
[Niko:] That's right we have a whole film crew here

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.440
Whole group of people that help us make our videos

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.500
and run a YouTube channel unlike any other YouTube channel on YouTube

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.960
and it's been quite an adventure, and it's time that we reflect that in the channels name

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:36.720
[Sam:] Exactly

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.460
The stories here that you see every day, it's...

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.700
You know, we're part of them, but everyone here is telling it you know

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.549
This is not like a crew in terms of like, just a group of friends

00:00:44.549 --> 00:00:48.040
But it's also a crew as far as being creative partners and collaborators

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.620
and working on content, and each other's ideas

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.620
[Niko:] So the videos are gonna stay the same, the same great videos that you know and love

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:57.100
[Sam:] And also I mean the banner picture looks pretty cool and we all look kind of badass. So...

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:57.980
I mean...

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.320
If you've been watching since 2011, you know the whole story of the channel already

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:05.080
But if you haven't, it's kind of interesting actually

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:08.820
It actually all started with Niko and myself just editing together

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.060
VFX breakdowns of our videos together

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.580
I still find it a little interesting every once in a while, to go back and check them out

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:19.060
Because that was when like, literally the Sam and Niko channel was the two of us filming videos together

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:19.760
Actually you know what?

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:20.940
Here's the-- here's the crazy thing

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.100
Every single person working together here in the studio right now

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.020
We've known each other for years through the weirdest...

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.220
weirdest ways

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.820
I don't know if you guys knew this, but actually

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:33.080
we first started working with Wren officially as he filmed behind the scenes for us

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.200
[Wren:] Back in the day, I was in college and I was like into YouTube and stuff

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.700
and the coolest channels - FreddieW and Corridor Digital

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.860
and I was doing my own visual effects at the time. And so they knew who I was

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:42.960
Niko knew who I was

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.000
So I was like hey, I'm in town

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.020
Everyone just happened to be outside at the time, and I was like there...

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.400
So what funny is that, Niko's like

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.540
"Sweet! See you there!"

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.620
but turns out Niko is in Minnesota at the time when he tweeted that back to me

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:54.120
[Laughs]

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:55.200
So I show up and uh...

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.700
the only person who knew I was gonna be there was Henry, from Minute Physics

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.760
I moved down to LA like, two months after that, and I worked on Sync

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.700
and then uh, they hired me to do behind the scenes

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.860
[Off screen Sam:] He was our first, you know experience, working with an editor

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.140
to kind of create vlog like stories

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.900
Then...the next great leap happened on the set of - Shadow of Mordor

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.320
Carmichael basically started joining the team

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:20.140
[Carmichael:] I worked at Star Citizen as their main behind-the-scenes person

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.640
RSVP to VHS season 2 premiere

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:26.000
where I met Sam and Niko, my good friend Spencer

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.360
Jake got me to work at Corridor here and there part-time

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.400
just sweeping floors, mopping floors, helping with shirts

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.900
[Sam:] Suddenly realize - wait a second, you know this dude edits...

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:39.360
[Carmichael:] Then I got offered by Jake to work for a week in Utah on the Shadow of Mordor

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.890
I did it. I came back. I got fired for doing it

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:43.880
Jake gave me a full-time job ever since

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.660
[Off screen Sam:] That was when Jake had that realization that like

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.020
Wait a second, these videos don't just need to be behind the scenes to be interesting!

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.340
We can tell stories that are

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:54.280
more than just the ones surrounding the content on the Corridor channel that we make

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.780
So it's really Carmichael and Jake that kind of helped us take that big push forward

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:58.360
With...

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.540
The help of Nick

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:04.720
We've known it for a long time actually too. 2011 when we first started our YouTube channel ah...

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.360
He actually helped shoot-- he shot half of our Minecraft video

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:11.680
[Nick:] I was mutual Facebook friends with, I think Niko, through Brett Driver

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.840
He like, posted a status back when people did that, saying

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.900
"Hey, we need a camera for this video we're shooting"

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.100
but I responded like, "Hey, I have a Canon 7D"

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.400
They're like cool bring it down

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.860
Yeah, it was the Minecraft video

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.380
[Off screen Carmichael:] Ohhh...

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.740
[Nick:] Oh.. No!

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.680
[Clap and Laughing]

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.360
I think I helped on Clock Blockers as well on camera

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.740
I didn't work with Sam and Niko during film school for about, two more years after that

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.120
Niko called me up for Snapper Hero to do editing, and then...

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.220
helped Carmichael once he started the vlogs. Then started doing it full-time

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:41.180
[Off screen Sam:] Christian was like the first person Jake met when he moved to Los Angeles

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.140
Or something like that

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:43.540
[Christian:] So when I first moved to LA

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:47.620
Jake was moving into the same complex. We became friends instantly, by being neighbors

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.160
He told me about this YouTube channel he was running with his friends

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.700
I ended up PA-ing on Gravity Gun and Rayman

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:58.380
and I actually production managed the Black Flag - Assassins Creed video

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.460
To help build this studio and build the sound room

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:03.880
I guess that's five or six years later. I'm here full time and

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.280
helping run all the brand stuff and producing all the videos

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:08.060
so, you know kind of came full circle

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.480
[Off screen Sam:] Adrian, straight up, was our Arch-nemesis in film competitions

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.660
on the internet before we met him in real life

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:17.720
[Adrian:] Yeah, I beat them every single time I entered any film competition

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.580
[Sam:] Like I was entering all these film contests and stuff

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:24.460
and I was seeing these other videos that were being entered to it that were just totally blowing ours away

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.080
(Whispers) I was like, "Who is this guy?"

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:29.100
[Adrian:] I think I hit up Sam-- I think he was having a wedding or something and I said

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:32.140
"Hey congratulations" and the Sam's like "Hey, do you want to meet up for lunch?"

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.460
I'm like "Yeah, sure - lets meet up for lunch"

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:36.960
Then we sat down and we actually got along really well and we had a lot of things in common

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.120
and then they were like, "Hey...

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.680
"...do you want to direct this Division series?"

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.220
No brainer. Hell yeah, and then from there they asked me to DP Battlefield Rush

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.460
and they they asked me to DP Lifeline

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.720
and every time we worked on projects together, we just had a really great time

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.120
[Off screen Sam:] Okay, so Gabe... I'd

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.560
Actually-- wait. I don't know his story

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.060
[Gabe:] My origin stories pretty simple

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.320
I worked on Snapper Hero. I walk into that door, and I was like

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.240
Wait...

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:58.600
I know this place

00:04:58.600 --> 00:04:59.780
Started freaking out

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.600
Inside...trying to keep it cool

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:02.700
[Off screen Sam:] Clint--

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:07.120
I video chatted with Clint back in like, 2011 too, before he even moved to Los Angeles

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:10.860
because he wanted a recommendation on what camera to buy, to shoot videos with

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:14.280
He was on skype with Freddy and we're all just like, talking about like, DSLR's and stuff

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.140
way back in the day.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.380
Crazy to think though how like, everyone here actually has

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.620
years of history despite all joining the team at different times, at different places

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:24.360
you know under different circumstances

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:28.100
The fact that we've been able to develop these relationships with all you guys and...

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.560
everyone in the studio here over the last few years, really...

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.680
Demonstrates the strength of this team

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:36.080
and it's something, more than any other video I've been working on...

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.500
I'm most proud of

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.360
So even though it might seem like a humongous deal that

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.840
we have changed the channel name and art and all this stuff

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:46.880
For us, as you've heard, it's one of the most natural steps we've ever done

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.140
[Niko:] So consider subscribing, if you haven't already

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.380
and stay tuned for a bunch more great Corridor content for the rest of the year

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.380
It's gonna be a good one

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:54.660
[Sam:] Do we-- do we?

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:56.320
Do we just call it Corridor content in general?

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.340
Or is it separate?

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:58.880
[Off screen Nick:] Crew-tent? Crew-tons?

00:05:58.880 --> 00:05:59.660
[Sam:] Crew-tons

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:00.160
[Giggles]

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:00.900
Oh wait!

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.800
[Off screen Nick:] Is that what our fan base is called?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.600
[Sam:] We're gonna call them the Crew-tons!

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:05.360
[Laughing]

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.520
[Niko:] Crew-tons

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:08.440
That's the worst idea ever heard--

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:09.660
[Off screen Nick:] Crew-tons!

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:11.060
[Sam:] Crew-tons

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.280
[Niko:] Guys stay tuned for the rest of the year as we come up with the great

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.440
names to call the people that watch this channel

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.780
[Sam:] Crew-tons

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:18.780
[Laughing]

